zing image patches</span></p></li></ul></li><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-par=
agraph"><strong><span>Output</span></strong><span>:</span></p><ul><li><p cl=
ass=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span>Saves heatmap visualizations to "anomal=
y_output" folder</span></p></li><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><spa=
n>Filename format: </span><code>{anomaly_score}_{original_name}.jpg</code><=
/p></li><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span>Includes original imag=
e, heatmap, and overlay in output</span></p></li></ul></li><li><p class=3D"=
ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong><span>Progress Tracking</span></strong><span=
>:</span></p><ul><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span>Uses tqdm for=
 progress bars during training and inference</span></p></li></ul></li></ol>=
<h2><span>Usage:</span></h2><ol start=3D"1"><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-par=
agraph"><span>Place normal training images in </span><code>images_train/</c=
ode><span> folder</span></p></li><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><sp=
an>Place test images in </span><code>images_All/</code><span> folder</span>=
</p></li><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span>Run the script</span>=
</p></li><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span>Check </span><code>an=
omaly_output/</code><span> for results</span></p></li></ol><p class=3D"ds-m=
arkdown-paragraph"><span>The anomaly score represents how different an imag=
e is from the normal training set, with higher scores indicating more anoma=
lous content. The heatmap shows which regions of the image contribute most =
to the anomaly score.</span></p></div></div><div class=3D"ds-theme" style=
